  "scope": "Executable native Fleet/bucket reference adapters, independent evidence checking and fresh same-image local observations; no equivalent-guarantee speedup or capacity qualification.",
  "implementation": [
    "Shared SQLite schema, statements and bindings for conditional sets, transfers, revision and payload data across Raft, Fleet and bucket.",
    "Native NodeFleet output gates with a bounded application transaction receipt: exact duplicate replay; conflict, expiry, sequence-gap and capacity refusal; no synthetic Raft tokens.",
    "One fsynced ledger and fixed open-loop scheduler, conservative ambiguity quarantine, fresh image/source/executable checks and capped local resource launchers.",
    "Independent baseline checker verifies raw serialized history and owner-route state/sequence. Aggregate native output proofs distinguish Fleet and bucket observations; a Fleet measurement with no Fleet proof is refused.",
    "Comparison reruns both analyzers and refuses a ratio when contracts, reads, hardware, workload or build records differ. CI runs the Python workload/evidence guards."
  ],
