  "limitations": [
    "Three 1-vCPU/3-GiB/no-swap Cellar containers per run plus RustFS in one owned Colima VM. Experiments ran sequentially; all exact containers exited zero and their volumes remain.",
    "The shared 32-GiB Mac had about 9.5 GiB swap in use before these runs. Other work was uncontrolled; no steady-state, causal speedup, instrumentation-overhead or independent-failure-domain result is claimed.",
    "Fleet and bucket reads route to owners, whereas the Raft runs verify actual follower reads and all replicas. Raft S3 additionally requires quorum/image publication. These contracts are not equivalent.",
    "The Quorum run retains one non-ambiguous VersionUnavailable follower-query response. Its submitted command histories reconcile; this observation does not close earlier read/transfer findings.",
    "Raft S3 misses the declared traffic objectives: 139/200 completed, 61 generator rejections and about 859ms p99 arrival latency.",
    "S3-compatible RustFS is not real Amazon S3 validation. Native restore tests use LocalStore; these physical measurements do not qualify disaster restore or slow-follower/failure behavior."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Investigate and improve Raft S3 archive acknowledgement latency using the retained owner measurements and unchanged durability checks.",
    "Add controlled slow-follower baselines, steady-state/overhead and full-device measurements, equivalent-contract analysis and density qualification.",
    "Q1 remains six processes and 10,000 three-voter cells (5,000 average replicas/process) versus the unchanged 4,096-group bound and the agreed five-node local ceiling.",
    "MR-13 remaining management/receipt/restore gates, earlier concurrent findings and MR-15 through MR-17 remain open."
  ]
